---
import Layout from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const kaomoji = { text: "<('.'-^)", label: "Waving Kirby" };
---

<Layout title="AI | João Palmeiro" description="How I use AI.">
  <header>
    <div class="flex justify-between">
      <h1>
        <span aria-hidden="true">~ </span>AI
      </h1>
      <span role="img" aria-label={kaomoji.label}>{kaomoji.text}</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <p>
      I use AI directly for two purposes: coding and searching. I use it via chat interfaces, easily integrating them
      into my workflow. This way, access is similar to other tools like my notes/repos and the Internet. The outcome is
      adequate.
    </p>

    <h2><span aria-hidden="true">~~ </span>Coding</h2>

    <ol class="list-inside list-decimal">
      <li>TODO</li>
      <li>TODO</li>
      <li>TODO</li>
    </ol>

    <h2><span aria-hidden="true">~~ </span>Searching</h2>

    <p>
      I turn to AI when I have something concrete I want to find and only have a vague description in mind. I only
      resort to it after trying to find what I'm looking for in a search engine first.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
